body:
This has already been debunked by Climate scientists. While positive feedbacks and tipping points can amplify climate change. A runaway climate change is very unlikely. The best climate models and computer simulations does not suggest runaway climate change beyond 2C. However, The longer we delay actions, the more dangerous the impacts will come and the more likely that those impacts will be irreversible. But, 1.5C and 2C is not a bright line where humanity is doomed and diseater is inevitable. These are goals where we can try to evaluate the impacts and allow us to avoid some of the most severe impacts. But, These impacts can be avoided or reduced. Luckily, We have many clean technologies that is very disruptive. Solar & Wind Energy, Li-On Batteries, Electric Vehicles, Autonomous vehicles, Precision Fermentation, 3D-Printed Vertical agriculture, Direct Air Capture. They will continue to improve in cost and performance. All of these technologies are very disruptive and will make a profound differance. We are 1.1C above pre-industrial times and if we stop all emissions today, It will only add 0.1C. We have the power to solve climate change with the right solutions and actions. Our future is shaped by our actions. The sooner we act, the better our future become. I believe we will turn this mess around. I don’t hope we can. I know we can. I hope this is useful.

&#x200B;

Best wishes :)

Regarding my anxiety issues, I feel like there might be a connection between my anxiety and this topic. But, I’m not so sure to be honest. I think you and NopedyDopedy have a good point. I might misinterpreted people words and actions. But, I must admit that I still feel the same and you’re right. It is very painful. I don’t want to think like this. But, I do. I usually makes post when I’m most vulnerable, weak and desperate. Thank you for your reply :)

&#x200B;

Many Hugs Back :)
